# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Industrial Vision Inspection HMI - V10

Key design change from V9:
- PRODUCT TRAINING IS LABELED BY THE USER.
- During TRAINING, the user explicitly selects/enters the product name.
- Every product gets its OWN folder and its OWN saved model file.
- There is NO unsupervised clustering of mixed images.
- During MONITORING, the user does NOT select the product; the system
  automatically identifies it from the learned product banks.

Pipeline:
    SAME CAMERA
       -> fixed ROI
       -> labeled GOOD product enrollment
       -> ResNet18 visual embedding for product identity
       -> per-product GOOD-only PatchCore-style detector + optional supervised defect classifier
       -> automatic product identification at inspection
       -> PASS / FAIL / UNKNOWN PRODUCT + KNOWN DEFECT
       -> SQLite + saved inspection image + ESP32 output

This version intentionally removes the old "automatic clustering" architecture and uses explicit per-product enrollment.
Defects are optionally learned per product from user-labeled GOOD/defect images.
When the operator knows which product is being enrolled, supervised enrollment
is more reliable and much easier to audit than trying to infer classes from an
unlabeled mixed folder.
"""

